  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Greener and Healthier Cities in Bahrain</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the project is to promote the transition toward more sustainable urban systems, improve environmental quality by increasing quality and use of green public spaces with direct effects on health and wellbeing of the residents in the Kingdom of Bahrain. The project is expected to strengthen capacities and improve the quality of selected green public spaces for Bahrainis. The project is aligned and will contribute to the National Plan for Afforestation (2022-2035), the Bahrain 2030 National Planning Development Strategy, the Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework signed in 2021, between United Nations and the Kingdom of Bahrain. It is aligned with FAO?s strategic framework (2022-2031), falling under the Better Environment and Better Life. It will contribute to the 2030 Sustainable Development Agenda, especially of Goal 11 on sustainable cites and Goal 2 on gender equality as well as the implementation of the New Urban Agenda in the Kingdom of Bahrain. The lessons learned will be disseminated and shared with other countries and cities within the Gulf Region and globally as an innovative and exemplary urban greening project.

The specific objectives of the project are: 1) Assess the current results and priorities in the implementation of the afforestation plan; 2) Improve and increase the availability, quality, and use of urban green public spaces and green</narrative>
  </description>
